        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "067552fc-ad13-5d8b-9f2d-cd73c448aed4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Princess and the Frog, The Frog Prince, The Frog Princess\n- People: E. D. Baker, Brothers Grimm, Jacob Grimm, Wilhelm Grimm, Rudolf Virchow, Claus von Stauffenberg, Adolf Hitler\n- Places: Alter St.-Matthäus-Kirchhof\n- Topics: fairy tales, Disney animated films\n\nFacts:\n- The Frog Prince; or, Iron Henry is a fairy tale traditionally placed first in the Brothers Grimm collection.\n- The Frog Prince is best known through the Brothers Grimm's written version.\n- The Princess and the Frog is the 49th Disney animated feature film.\n- The Princess and the Frog is loosely based on E. D. Baker's novel The Frog Princess.\n- E. D. Baker's novel The Frog Princess is in turn based on the Brothers Grimm fairy tale The Frog Prince.\n- Alter St.-Matthäus-Kirchhof is known as the burial place of Brothers Grimm members Jacob Grimm and Wilhelm Grimm.\n- Alter St.-Matthäus-Kirchhof is also known for the interment of Rudolf Virchow.\n- Alter St.-Matthäus-Kirchhof is also known for the interment of Claus von Stauffenberg, a German Army officer who nearly assassinated Adolf Hitler.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "806de8ca-5770-5ff7-8738-d024002e1684",
        "text": "Page: The Princess and the Frog. Sentence: The 49th Disney animated feature film, the film is loosely based on the novel \"The Frog Princess\" by E. D. Baker, which is in turn based on the Brothers Grimm fairy tale \"The Frog Prince\".\nPage: The Frog Prince. Sentence: \"The Frog Prince; or, Iron Henry\" (German: \"Der Froschkönig oder der eisen Heinrich\" , literally \"The Frog King; or, The Iron Heinrich\") is a fairy tale, best known through the Brothers Grimm's written version; traditionally it is the first story in their collection.\nPage: Alter St.-Matthäus-Kirchhof. Sentence: It is known for its interment of the Brothers Grimm, Jacob and Wilhelm Grimm, folklore tellers of \"Cinderella\" (\"Aschenputtel\"), \"The Frog Prince\" (\"Der Froschkönig\"), \"Hansel and Gretel\" (\"Hänsel und Gretel\"), \"Rapunzel\", \"Rumpelstiltskin\" (\"Rumpelstilzchen\"), and \"Snow White\" (\"Schneewittchen\"); Rudolf Virchow, variously known as \"father of modern pathology\", \"father of modern medicine\" or \"father of social medicine\"; and Claus von Stauffenberg, a German Army officer who almost assassinated Adolf Hitler.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
